                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1c61de0-684b-3ecc-a609-67f7f8774e3f",
                        "entry_id": "eb5713a3-3f8f-30dd-9a78-d827492d2f29",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Kamel mit einem Höcker"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e931781-63dd-4d41-9649-cd977b9445c5",
                                "sense_id": "b1c61de0-684b-3ecc-a609-67f7f8774e3f",
                                "text": "„Wo genau wilde Dromedare lebten und wann sie ausstarben, ist noch nicht restlos geklärt.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "682830f0-e420-4d35-9a97-be00226a0293",
                                "sense_id": "b1c61de0-684b-3ecc-a609-67f7f8774e3f",
                                "text": "„Die von uns entsandten Boten kehrten nach fünfzehn Tagen mit acht Dromedaren zurück.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c95d2ced-8568-4ca0-82cd-914ac8dc3472",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb5713a3-3f8f-30dd-9a78-d827492d2f29",
                        "source_sense_id": "b1c61de0-684b-3ecc-a609-67f7f8774e3f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zoologie: Kamel mit einem Höcker",
                        "target_lang_word": "Arabian camel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Arabian camel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d775b082-62eb-3b74-a544-f92fa18ab30a",
                                        "entry_id": "d06a722f-6345-3927-b6d0-5be9e3cb2173",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The dromedary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2d4b4a60-eb84-4473-a8bf-162970227694",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb5713a3-3f8f-30dd-9a78-d827492d2f29",
                        "source_sense_id": "b1c61de0-684b-3ecc-a609-67f7f8774e3f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zoologie: Kamel mit einem Höcker",
                        "target_lang_word": "dromedary",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dromedary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e5594ca5-99da-3223-8796-523833abc987",
                                        "entry_id": "b237f7a7-1efa-3a40-9373-0ca1ca35ec42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The single-humped camel (Camelus dromedarius)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3ef1356-ccf0-470e-8d4d-875c8da302a2",
                                                "sense_id": "e5594ca5-99da-3223-8796-523833abc987",
                                                "text": "The duke in his schelde and dreches no lengere, / Drawes hym a dromedarie, with dredfulle knyghtez; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b58034fa-cb3b-44f4-ba2b-ddbe36b46bf5",
                                                "sense_id": "e5594ca5-99da-3223-8796-523833abc987",
                                                "text": "The Dromedarie, Camell, Horſe, and Aſſe, / For loade and carriage doth a Sheepe ſurpaſſe: [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78353eab-0868-42c9-b1e6-6249b8390c28",
                                                "sense_id": "e5594ca5-99da-3223-8796-523833abc987",
                                                "text": "[T]he Dromedarie [...] who is marvellous ſwift, and will run an hundred miles in a day; but the Germanes call a dull and ſlow man a Dromedary, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ca2618d-f2f2-423c-8e13-ea58a771731d",
                                                "sense_id": "e5594ca5-99da-3223-8796-523833abc987",
                                                "text": "I went to see a Dromedarie, a very monstrous beaste, much like the Camel but larger."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f89cd46-1055-4eec-8f81-ef11458030e9",
                                                "sense_id": "e5594ca5-99da-3223-8796-523833abc987",
                                                "text": "Oh, thou Dromedary, thou Founder'd Mule, without a Pack-ſaddle; or what other foul Beaſt ſhall I call thee, for Man thou art not, nor haſt not been to me, Heaven knows the time when? Art not thou aſham'd to ſee me, thou Nincompoop?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3657515-e563-4b0a-beec-7534a299454b",
                                                "sense_id": "e5594ca5-99da-3223-8796-523833abc987",
                                                "text": "Here we alighted, drank ourſelves, and gave our dromedaries to drink as much as they would; then we filled all our veſſels, made on purpoſe for carriage, and took in a much greater proportion of water than we had done proviſions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ed9c7d1-b1a4-4aaa-a8ee-eb0f983d32ca",
                                                "sense_id": "e5594ca5-99da-3223-8796-523833abc987",
                                                "text": "[T]he camel has two bunches upon his back, whereas the dromedary has but one; the latter alſo, is neither ſo large, nor ſo ſtrong, as the camel. Theſe two races, however, produce with each other, and the mixed breed formed between them is conſidered the beſt, the moſt patient, and the moſt indefatigable of all the kind."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb7eb8a0-4d11-343c-9ee6-9dcd2ef8f52b",
                                        "entry_id": "b237f7a7-1efa-3a40-9373-0ca1ca35ec42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any swift riding camel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04349cea-56e2-4f09-9195-32b54cecd252",
                                                "sense_id": "cb7eb8a0-4d11-343c-9ee6-9dcd2ef8f52b",
                                                "text": "[T]hou art like a ſwift dromedarie, that runneth by his wayes.",
                                                "translation": "Thou art like a swift dromedary, that runs in his ways.",
                                                "english": "Thou art like a swift dromedary, that runs in his ways."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15a6717c-e9a1-305c-9dcb-b0e32dcdf5d9",
                                        "entry_id": "b237f7a7-1efa-3a40-9373-0ca1ca35ec42",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Referring to a biphasic clinical course of poliomyelitis, typically occurring in children, characterized by a minor illness, followed by an asymptomatic period of several days before the onset of a major illness involving the central nervous system."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "attributive",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec266be2-9ff6-48a0-9ed7-c2b5fa7991bb",
                                                "sense_id": "15a6717c-e9a1-305c-9dcb-b0e32dcdf5d9",
                                                "text": "The untreated cases have been arranged in three groups according to the clinical course. The first group, called the dromedary group, shows the curious phenomenon of two different periods of illness with an interval of well-being. […] Because of the two distinct groups or humps of symptoms, the analogy to the arrangement of the dromedary’s back was taken to express the type figuratively."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "adf76865-982d-43ba-8236-6f783291dfe1",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb5713a3-3f8f-30dd-9a78-d827492d2f29",
                        "source_sense_id": "b1c61de0-684b-3ecc-a609-67f7f8774e3f",
